      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Over three years of individual audio sliders being requested multiple times and its not even implemented in a persistent manner. How much time was actually spent implementing this highly requested feature?\nThe ability to choose who is persistent or even just do friends would suffice at this point. Also save it locally, we dont expect you to save everything on our account if you apparently dont want to, seeing as you didnt implement this with persistence anyway.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-12-10T00:53:53.409Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think it would be nice to have an option that would allow you to save people's voice volume sliders across play sessions. Some people are just naturally loud or quiet and everyone has different mics. Telling someone to change their mic volume if it's a repeat issue kind of defeats the entire purpose of the being able to lower and raise their volume if you have to resort to doing that instead. It will get pretty tiring having to keep constantly changing people's sliders every single time I log on and join a 30 person instance",
